> I tried according to the solution by adding "se = "bootstrap"

Your example calculates indirect effects.  If you are trying to use bootstrapping for inference, then you should be aware that setting se="bootstrap" still assumes a normal sampling distribution.  Only the SE estimate itself is calculated from the empirical bootstrap distribution.  You can use this package <https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/semhelpinghands/vignettes/standardizedSolution_boot_ci.html> to obtain bootstrap CI, which is the usual recommendation.  Alternatively, a parametric bootstrap is available in the semTools package (see the ?monteCarloCI help page for examples and a reference to read).

> it still does not work.

What do you mean "does not work"?  Please provide your output, or ideally a reprex <https://stackoverflow.com/help/minimal-reproducible-example> so someone is able to try tracking down the issue.

