Subject: Syntax for multiple group moderated mediation analysis
Message-ID: <PbrUEksGT9I.96pIme65AgAJ@lavaan.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/lavaan/c/PbrUEksGT9I/m/96pIme65AgAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Dear all, I am trying to run a multiple group path analysis (all variables are observed variables) in lavaan for a moderated mediation model. IV, DV and moderator are dichotomous, the mediator is continuous. I provide example data / the code below.

My questions:
(overarching:) Is the model syntax correct?
Particularly the interaction; does it work like this for two dichotomous variables as well?
Is using DWLS correct?

Any pointers to literature that answers my questions, or direct replies are very much appreciated! Thanks for your time,

Sophie

------

set.seed(123)

###sample data
n <- 1000

group <- rbinom(n, 1, prob = 0.45)
IV <- rbinom(n, 1, prob = 0.5)
mod <- rbinom(n, 1, prob = 0.4)

med <- rnorm(n, mean = 10 + 5 * IV, sd = 3)
med <- pmin(pmax(med, 0), 20)

logit_DV <- -5 + 0.3 * med + 0.1 * mod
prob_DV <- 1 / (1 + exp(-logit_DV))
DV <- rbinom(n, 1, prob = prob_DV)

df <- data.frame(group, IV, mod, med, DV)

###path model
library(lavaan)

simmodel_wi <- '
  med ~ c(a1g1, a1g2)*IV + c(a2g1, a2g2)*mod + c(a3g1, a3g2)*IV:mod

  DV ~ c(c1g1, c1g2)*IV + c(b1g1, b1g2)*med + c(c3g1, c3g2)*mod + c(c4g1, c4g2)*IV:mod

  #indirect effects
  ind_g1 := a1g1 * b1g1
  ind_g2 := a1g2 * b1g2

  #direct effects
  direct_g1 := c1g1
  direct_g2 := c1g2

  #total effects
  total_g1 := direct_g1 + ind_g1
  total_g2 := direct_g2 + ind_g2
'

fit_simmodel_wi <- sem(simmodel_wi, df, group = "group", ordered = "DV", estimator = "DWLS", link = "probit", se = "bootstrap", bootstrap = 1000)
summary(fit_simmodel_wi, fit.measures = TRUE, standardize = TRUE, rsquare=TRUE, estimates = TRUE, ci = TRUE)

